+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Physical MAIN authorization plus engagement or active lateral control and target/actual speeds of at least 30 km/h must persist for 0.5 seconds before SET−. Gas release after standby acceleration uses a 0.1s confirmation and SET− at current speed. Actual stock engagement synchronizes MAIN tracking without restoring revoked authorization.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+After turning ON, restart and physically operate MAIN. Brake, CANCEL, MAIN OFF or observation gaps revoke authorization; cycle MAIN OFF then ON to rearm.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Below 30 km/h actual speed, the driver must accelerate. No direct braking or standstill launch; stock-vehicle acceptance requires vehicle validation.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
